---
title: States of the DID controller (Stuart) - create, update, and deactivate
---

%% One state machine for the DID controller side of the key rotation use cases.
%% The Aggregation Participant states are in states-aggregation-participant.mmd.
%% Rule: only one update is in flight. A new update starts only after the last one has minConf confirmations.

stateDiagram-v2
    state "DID created (version 1)<br/>offline, no Bitcoin transaction" as Created
    state "Idle: version N is settled" as Idle
    state "Resolve own DID (minConf 6)<br/>versionId = N" as Resolving
    state "Construct BTCR2 Unsigned Update<br/>targetVersionId = N + 1" as Unsigned
    state "Construct BTCR2 Signed Update<br/>(signer, capabilityInvocation key)" as Signed
    state "Verify update.proof" as Verify
    state beacon <<choice>>
    state "Build and sign the Beacon Signal<br/>(Beacon Address key), broadcast" as SingletonTx
    state "Wait for the next aggregation round<br/>(see Aggregation Participant states)" as Round
    state "Pending: Beacon Signal has fewer than<br/>minConf confirmations" as Pending
    state "Settled: version N + 1" as Settled
    state "Distribute: publish to CAS,<br/>or keep for the Sidecar Data (life of the DID)" as Distribute
    state "Deactivated (permanent)" as Deactivated

    [*] --> Created: create(genesisBytes, network, version)
    Created --> Idle: keep the Genesis Document (x1 DID)

    Idle --> Resolving: new key material, or other change
    Resolving --> Idle: resolution error (fix it first)
    Resolving --> Unsigned: jsonPatch
    Unsigned --> Idle: INVALID_DID_UPDATE (fix the patch)
    Unsigned --> Signed
    Signed --> Idle: INVALID_DID_UPDATE (no capabilityInvocation key)
    Signed --> Verify
    Verify --> Idle: proof does not verify (never announce it)
    Verify --> beacon: proof verifies

    beacon --> SingletonTx: Singleton Beacon
    beacon --> Round: CAS Beacon or SMT Beacon
    SingletonTx --> Pending: broadcast
    Round --> Round: round failed (respond again)
    Round --> Pending: round Beacon Signal broadcast
    Pending --> SingletonTx: transaction dropped (Singleton Beacon, same Signal Bytes)
    Pending --> Settled: minConf confirmations

    Settled --> Distribute
    Distribute --> Idle: send the did and Sidecar Data to peers
    Distribute --> Deactivated: the update added deactivated = true
    Deactivated --> [*]

    note right of Pending
        Do not construct the next update in this state.
        A fresh resolution at minConf 6 still returns version N,
        so the next update would reuse targetVersionId N + 1.
        Two different updates with one targetVersionId
        make the DID fail with LATE_PUBLISHING.
    end note
